WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A weekend plan changes: arrival moves to Saturday and one more guest is joining.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Ripple checks this fictional plan through its real browser client and local MCP server.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Seven changes are proposed. The restaurant cancellation shows its simulated $75 fee before approval.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:16.000
I approve only the reviewed operation. The server records consent, but nothing executes yet.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:40.000
Approval and execution are separate. I now execute that one approved change.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:59.000
The server reports six live commitments, a simulated $75 fee, and six open decisions.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:15.000
Fictional services and simulated fees only: no real booking, charge, Alexa runtime, or Alexa integration.
